gold: lmbda ramp window, generation floor, stop_at_step

Applies to: github.com/laminair/gb-steps-distillation at
            288bfc6bdab589eca394ca9f7229f1138a6da1c4 -- the commit
            lmbda_linear_schedule.diff produces from a5d59bc4 -- from the checkout ROOT:

              git -C <checkout> apply steps/distill/gold/skypilot/patches/onpolicy_study.diff

            git apply skips this header.

Four CustomGOLDConfig fields, each needed by an arm of the on-policy study
(recipes/granite4-350m/lsf/distill-onpolicy-switch-study). Every one defaults to the
behaviour of 288bfc6b, so a run that leaves them alone trains exactly as it did there.

  lmbda_ramp_start_step, lmbda_ramp_steps
      The linear schedule ramped over global_step / max_steps, so it could neither ramp
      over part of a run (0 -> 1 over the first half, then 1) nor start at a resumed run's
      own first step (a run resumed at 2,000 of an 8,150-step schedule began its ramp at
      0.25 of the way up). The ramp now runs from lmbda_ramp_start_step for
      lmbda_ramp_steps steps, 0 meaning "until max_steps".

  min_completion_length
      The generation floor. trl 0.26.2's vllm_serve merges a request's generation_kwargs
      into SamplingParams last, so the trainer sends {"min_tokens": N} with every server
      request and the floor needs no server-side patch. Colocate mode sets
      SamplingParams.min_tokens directly. 0 sends nothing.

  stop_at_step
      Save and stop at a fixed step while leaving max_steps -- and with it the LR
      schedule's shape -- alone. A resume of an 8,150-step run that should train 2,500
      more steps cannot lower max_steps without reshaping the schedule it restores.

Verified 2026-10-11 on stubs of the patched methods: the defaults reproduce
0.25 / 0.3125 / 0.375 / 0.4375 / 0.5 at steps 0 / 625 / 1250 / 1875 / 2500 for 0.25 -> 0.5
over 2,500; ramp (0, 1250) gives 0 / 0.5 / 1 / 1 at 0 / 625 / 1250 / 2500; ramp
(2000, 2500) on an 8,150-step schedule gives 0 / 0.5 / 1 at 2000 / 3250 / 4500.

